OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGJOURNALISTS HAND IN LETTER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTO IRAQ EMBASSY
OL,4,F
OL,5, Observer editor Donald Trelford has
OL,6, handed in a letter at the Iraqi embassy
OL,7, in London pleading for the life of one
OL,8, of his reporters, Farzad Bazoft.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe Iraqi foreign ministry has already
OL,11,Fagreed to pass on a plea for clemency
OL,12,Ffrom Mrs Thatcher.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FBritain's ambassador to Iraq, Harold
OL,15,FWalker, delivered her request today.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FMr Bazoft has been sentenced to death
OL,18,Fon spying charges. Mrs Daphne Parish,
OL,19,Fwho was accused of helping him, was
OL,20,Fimprisoned for 15 years.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG11-03-90
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
