OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773231702
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/10
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGLITHUANIAN PARLIAMENT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGASSERTS SOVEREIGNTY
OL,4,D
OL,5, In the USSR, the parliament of the
OL,6, republic of Lithuania has voted for a
OL,7, declaration that the country's
OL,8, sovereignty has been "re-instated".
OL,10,FThis sovereignty was curtailed by
OL,11,Fforeign powers tn 1940, said the
OL,12,Fparliament's declaration - a reference
OL,13,Fto annexation by the USSR.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FEarlier, non-Communist Vytautas
OL,16,FLandsbergis, leader of the Sajudis
OL,17,Fnationalist movement, was elected
OL,18,Fpresident.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe republic's name has also been
OL,21,Fchanged, dropping the title "Soviet".
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG11-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
