OL,1,Vk4                               G7/10
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGCHILE'S NEW PRESIDENT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSWORN IN
OL,4,D
OL,5, Chile's new president, Patricio Aylwin,
OL,6, has been sworn in, replacing long-time
OL,7, dictator General Augusto Pinochet.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FAylwin, a 71-year-old lawyer, won 55%
OL,10,Fof the vote in presidential elections
OL,11,Flast December, beating a former
OL,12,Fminister under Pinochet.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FPinochet came to power in a bloody
OL,15,Fmilitary coup in 1973 that toppled the
OL,16,Felected government of Marxist president
OL,17,FSalvador Allende.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FHe says he will continue as commander
OL,20,Fof the army, despite requests by Aylwin
OL,21,Fthat he retire.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG11-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
